.Dd October 5, 2026
.Dt JOB.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm job.conf
.Nd job service configuration
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The service reads a versioned TOML document.
Unknown keys and unsupported schema versions are errors.
The current schema accepts these fields:
.Bl -tag -width schema_version
.It Cm schema_version
Required integer, currently 1.
.It Cm profile
Either ordinary (the default) or legacy.
.It Cm presets.classes
Optional array of named admission classes.
Each requires name, positive integer revision and priority from -1000 through 1000.
Classes cannot set kernel resource weights or limits.
.It Cm presets.profiles
Optional array of execution profiles with name and positive integer revision.
Optional extends is an ordered array of parent references, each NAME@REV.
Optional scheduling_class selects NAME@REV or none.
Optional values contains independent resource fields (CPU in millicores,
memory in bytes), pids, wall_ms, confine, or net equal to Host, None,
profile:NAME or ns:NAME, where NAME is defined under network.
Parents apply in order, followed by the profile's own fields.
There are no implicit profile selections.
.It Cm network.namespace_directory
Optional absolute directory in which a namespace without an absolute path is
looked up;
.Pa /run/netns
by default.
.It Cm network.namespaces. Ns Ar NAME
Optional table that authorizes an existing network namespace for
.Fl -net Cm ns:NAME .
A client can select only what is named here.
Optional path is the namespace file: absolute, or relative to
namespace_directory, and
.Ar NAME
in that directory when absent. A path under
.Pa /proc
or with a .. component is refused.
Optional user_namespace is the file of the user namespace that owns it, which
the service joins first; an ordinary-user service needs it.
Optional resolv_conf is a file the Job sees as
.Pa /etc/resolv.conf .
Optional description is shown by
.Cm job net show .
At most 64 namespaces. Names use letters, digits, - and _.
.It Cm network.profiles. Ns Ar NAME
Optional table that defines a routing profile for
.Fl -net Cm profile:NAME .
Required egress is host, none, socks5://HOST:PORT, http://HOST:PORT,
https://HOST:PORT, wireguard:/ABSOLUTE/FILE or ns:NAME; a user and password
inside it are refused.
Optional secret_file, for a proxy only, is an absolute path to a file with
USER:PASSWORD that belongs to the service user and has mode 600.
Optional bandwidth is the rate each way for the profile's whole network, and
job_bandwidth for each Job, for example 10Mbit.
Optional dns is an array of at most three IPv4 resolver addresses.
Optional allow and deny are arrays of at most 64 rules each, written
ADDRESS[/PREFIX][:PORT[-PORT]][/tcp|/udp] with IPv4 addresses; deny wins, and
allow narrows what the egress forwards. An IPv6 range is refused.
Optional sharing is per-job (the default), per-queue or shared.
Optional description is shown by
.Cm job net show .
With a proxy, dns, allow and deny are refused; with none or ns:NAME every other
key but description is refused. At most 64 profiles.
.It Cm pressure
Optional array of host pressure rules; absent or empty enables none.
Each rule requires id, resource (cpu, memory or io), metric (some or full),
window (avg10, avg60 or avg300), high_bp, low_bp, sustain_ms,
minimum_hold_ms, recovery_ms, step_ms and required (boolean).
Thresholds are integer basis points from 0 through 10000, with low strictly below high.
Host CPU full is invalid.
Each duration is an integer from 1000 through 9223372036854775807 milliseconds.
Rule IDs contain 1 through 64 ASCII letters, digits, hyphens or underscores;
IDs must be unique within the array, which accepts at most 32 rules.
There are no implicit thresholds or timing values.
.It Cm output
Optional table. head_bytes and tail_bytes are service defaults for the output
quota of each recorded stream, between 1M and 1G; a Queue, Group, profile or Job
value takes precedence. Absent values leave the built-in retention.
budget_bytes bounds all recordings of the service together and defaults to 1G;
completed recordings are removed oldest first while the total is above it.
Each value is an integer number of bytes or a string such as "4M".
.It Cm terminal
Optional table. detach_key is the key an attached client detaches with when
neither its option nor
.Ev JOB_DETACH_KEY
names one: ctrl- followed by a letter or one of ], \e, ^ and _, or none.
The default is ctrl-].
.It Cm socket.group
Optional name or numeric ID of one Unix group that shares the service socket.
Absent, the socket is private to the service user.
When set, the runtime directory gets mode 0750 and the socket mode 0660, both
owned by the group, and a peer whose primary or supplementary groups contain
it is admitted beside the service user.
The service user must be a member, and the socket must lie in a runtime
directory apart from the state directory.
An unknown group stops the start.
Work still runs as the service user, and the state directory stays private.
Members get output from the service over the socket, and the terminal sockets
of running Jobs are placed in
.Pa terminals/
below the runtime directory with the same group rule.
.It Cm cgroup.root
Optional absolute path of the cgroup v2 directory the service manages.
.Ev JOB_CGROUP_ROOT
takes precedence.
Absent, the service discovers the delegated cgroup it was started in.
A named root that holds other processes stops the start.
.It Cm cgroup.required
Optional boolean, false by default.
When true, the service refuses to start without a usable delegated cgroup and
names what is missing.
When false and no cgroup is found, the service starts in monitoring mode:
limits are watched, not enforced, and the start line,
.Cm job host
and
.Cm job doctor
say so.
In monitoring mode with the ordinary profile a Job that asks for
.Fl -mem ,
.Fl -pids
or a cgroup control is refused with a capability error; the legacy profile
keeps watching
.Fl -mem
and
.Fl -pids .
A change takes effect at the next restart.
.It Cm events.keep_files , Cm events.rotate_bytes
Optional retention of the lifecycle event journal read by
.Cm job events :
how many files are kept, 8 by default, and the size at which the current file
is closed, 8388608 bytes by default.
Both must be at least 1.
.Cm job config reload
applies a change.
.El
.Pp
The ordinary profile uses only explicit resource requests for admission.
It does not synthesize resource estimates, reserve future backfill slots,
limit process counts, disable swap or terminate work for host pressure.
Explicit controls and enclosing operating-system limits still apply.
Legacy command-line resource options retain their existing semantics.
Explicit pressure rules gate new starts regardless of compatibility profile,
without terminating or suspending running work.
Their transient concurrency ceiling is separate from saved configuration.
The legacy profile's emergency termination remains a separate compatibility policy.
.Pp
The legacy profile preserves automatic estimation, conservative backfilling,
the default process limit, swap restriction and emergency host protection.
It is a compatibility choice for an existing installation.
.Sh FILES
Configuration is selected by
.Ev JOB_CONFIG
when set; otherwise by
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/job/config.toml
or
.Pa ~/.config/job/config.toml
for a user service, and by
.Pa /etc/job/config.toml
for a system service.
When no location can be derived the command fails and names the variable to set.
A missing default file selects ordinary behavior for fresh state.
A missing explicitly selected file is an error.
Legacy state requires an explicit configuration.
.Sh COMMAND POLICY
The command policy is a separate file,
.Pa policy.json ,
in the same directory as the configuration:
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/job/policy.json
or
.Pa ~/.config/job/policy.json
for a user, and
.Pa /etc/job/policy.json
for the system.
A user's own file is used when it exists, otherwise the system's; the two
are never merged.
When
.Ev JOB_CONFIG
is set, only
.Pa policy.json
beside the named configuration is read.
.Pp
job ships no rules.
Without a file the policy is empty and forbids nothing.
The file is read by
.Cm job hook
and
.Cm job policy
each time they run, so a change takes effect with the next command that is
checked; the service does not read it and nothing is reloaded.
.Pp
The file is one JSON object.
Every field is optional and an unknown field is an error.
.Bl -tag -width protected_paths
.It Cm rules
Object.
Each key is the name of a rule, each value an object with the texts
.Cm forbids
and
.Cm instead ,
which make up the refusal.
A rule that is not named is not in force.
.It Cm protected_paths
Array of strings: the operands the rule rm-protected guards.
.It Cm work_root
Absolute directory whose entries each belong to the caller of the same name.
.It Cm repos_root
Absolute directory of shared checkouts that belong to no caller.
.It Cm sudo_callers
Array of caller names the rule sudo lets through.
.It Cm push
Array of objects with
.Cm caller
and
.Cm remotes ,
the remote names the rule git-push lets that caller push to.
.El
.Pp
The rules are:
.Bl -tag -width rm-recursive-force
.It Cm rm-recursive-force
rm with both a recursive and a force flag.
.It Cm rm-protected
A recursive rm of an operand in protected_paths.
.It Cm empty-variable
A destructive command (rm, mv, truncate, shred, recursive cp, chmod and chown,
dd of=, find -delete) whose path holds a variable or substitution not written
as ${NAME:?}.
.It Cm find-root
find starting at /.
.It Cm kill-by-pattern
pkill and killall.
.It Cm no-verify
git with --no-verify, and git commit -n.
.It Cm pipe-to-shell
A download with curl or wget piped into a shell.
.It Cm sudo
sudo and doas, unless the caller's name is in sudo_callers.
.It Cm git-push
git push, unless push names the caller and the remote.
.It Cm other-worktree
A git command that changes state under repos_root, or under an entry of
work_root that does not carry the caller's name.
.El
.Pp
.Cm job policy Fl -show
prints the file in use and the rules in force and validates the file;
.Cm job doctor
reports the same.
While a file is invalid,
.Cm job policy
fails and
.Cm job hook
refuses every command with the reason.
.Pp
A policy with two rules:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
  "rules": {
    "find-root": {
      "forbids": "find starting at /",
      "instead": "find in the one directory you mean"
    },
    "pipe-to-shell": {
      "forbids": "a download piped into a shell",
      "instead": "download to a file, read it, then run it"
    }
  }
}
.Ed
.Sh VALIDATION AND RELOAD
.Cm job config check Ar file
validates a file without contacting the service.
.Cm job config init Fl -profile Cm ordinary | legacy Ar file
creates a file with owner-only permissions and refuses to overwrite one.
.Cm job config show Fl -json
shows the running configuration, its source and enabled compatibility rules.
.Pp
.Cm job config reload
requires no active or queued Jobs and cannot change the profile,
the socket group, the cgroup root or
.Cm cgroup.required .
To switch profile, finish or cancel existing Jobs, stop the service,
change configuration, and restart.
Recovery refuses active records from a different profile.
.Pp
Accepted preset revisions are immutable; changing a definition requires a new revision.
Reload refuses removal of definitions still selected by a Queue or Group.
The historical archive retains removed definitions for attempt validation.
Active configuration permits 128 definitions; the archive permits 4096 definitions
and 16 MiB of JSON. Composition permits 16 parents, 16 levels and 1024 visits.
.Pp
Network namespaces and routing profiles are not versioned. A Job resolves the
name when it starts and records the digest of the profile it used. Reading a
configuration fails, at start and at reload, when a Queue, a Group or an
execution profile names a namespace or routing profile that it does not define.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
schema_version = 1
profile = "ordinary"

[socket]
group = "jobusers"

[network.namespaces.lab]
description = "the measurement bench"

[network.profiles.updates]
egress = "host"
allow = ["192.0.2.10:443/tcp", "192.0.2.53:53"]
dns = ["192.0.2.53"]
bandwidth = "20Mbit"
sharing = "shared"
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr job 1 ,
.Xr job 7 ,
.Xr jobd 8
